The new ePump code depends on the ROOT, LHAPDF, and Eigen3 packages, before compiling the ePump code, please install ROOT, LHAPDF, and Eigen3 at first.

For LHAPDF,

Download page: [https://lhapdf.hepforge.org/downloads/](https://lhapdf.hepforge.org/downloads/)

Installation:

./configure --prefix=/path to install
make -j16
make install

[IMPORTANT] Do not forget add the following line to your environment

export LHAPDF_ROOT_DIR=/path to LHAPDF/

For Eigen3,

Download page: [https://gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen](https://gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen)

Installation:

mkdir build
cd build
cmake .. -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=.
make -j16
make install

The new ePump code also provides the Python interface, if you have installed the Python, you can turn on the Python flag from the CMakeLists.txt:
set(USE_PYTHON ON)

For compiling the ePump code, usage:

mkdir build
cd build
cmake ..
make -j install

Add PATH and LD_LIBRARY_PATH to your environment

export PATH=${PATH}:/path to ePumpAP/build/bin
export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=${LD_LIBRARY_PATH}:/path to ePumpAP/build/lib

If you turn on the Python flag, before using the Python interface, do not forget add the following lines to your PYTHONPATH

export PYTHONPATH=$PYTHONPATH:/path to ePumpAP/build/bin



